# s710_runtime_part2.oot — (Part 2 of s710_runtime.oot)
# Continuation of `openOODA/audit/s710_runtime.oot`.

---

### Source (.oo) — PASS
`c_parse_secret_env` (`ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret.oo` L7–82 after Domain A):

- L8: needle `"// " + "SECRET:"` — **one** literal concat (not the leak).
- L13–32: line-start + exact needle.
- L34–42: skip space/tab with `char_at`.
- L43: `let start = k;`
- L44–64: advance `k` while `is_al` (`_` / A–Z / a–z / 0–9; leading
  digits still accepted — pre-existing, not 7.1 start-vs-cont).
- **L65:** `let name = str_slice(src, start, k);`
- **No** `name = name + c`.
- **No** `char buf[N]` (language has no stack `char[]` in `.oo`).
- L70 / L72: `c_env_put` prefix concat of the **finished** name.

SPRINT “char-by-char leak” = do not rebuild the SECRET ident with
per-char `OoStr` concat **and** do not cap it in a fixed C array.
Alpha close = **one slice per directive name** (same as 7.1 ident /
7.2 last-arg). Domain A landed that in source.

`chs_rt*.c` still has many `char buf[N]` (crypto, PATH_MAX, sprintf
int). Those are **other floor** — not this walk.

### Product machine code — FAIL residual (stale; not a post-slice ELF)
`objdump` of `c_parse_secret_env` (3378 B @ `0x45d140`):

| Callee | Count | Role |
|--------|------:|------|
| `oo_str_lit` | 78 | letter / digit / punct / empty / prefixes |
| `oo_str_eq` | 68 | same classification |
| `oo_str_release` | 8 | stored `OoStr` temps |
| `oo_char_at` | 5 | line-start / needle / space / class |
| `oo_str_concat` | **4** | needle; **ident loop**; `__sec__`; `__secref__` |
| `oo_chars_len` | 2 | `nn` / `sn` |
| `c_env_put` | 2 | `__sec__` + `__secref__` |
| `oo_str_retain` | 1 | return `env` |
| `oo_print_str` / `oo_println` / `exit@plt` | 1 each | empty-name fail-closed |
| `oo_str_slice` | **0** | — |

Ident-loop leak (pre-slice) at `0x45d3a0`–`0x45d3d3`:

```
add    $0x1, %r12          ; k = k + 1
call   oo_str_concat       ; name = name + c
call   oo_str_release      ; drop old name
call   oo_str_release      ; drop c
```

That pair is **exactly** `name = name + c`. Source no longer has it.

Honest (non-leak) concats on this ELF, which **will remain** after a
correct rebuild:

- `0x45d17a` — `"// " + "SECRET:"` (L8)
- `0x45dd28` — `"__sec__" + name` then `c_env_put` (L70)
- `0x45dd97` — `"__secref__" + name` then `c_env_put` (L72)

- **Zero** `sprintf` / `strncpy` / `strcpy` / `strcat` / `memcpy` / `malloc`
  inside this function.
- Entry: `sub $0x68, %rsp` — 104-byte spill frame for `OoStr` pairs +
  callee-saves, **not** a `char ident[N]`.
- `char` text in the dump is only `oo_char_at` / `oo_chars_len` names.

So: host is **not** a stack-buffer rewrite; it is the **old concat
walker**. `char[N]` is not how 7.10 leaked and is not how the stale
ELF still leaks.

### Seed ELF contrast — honesty (not the product host)
`ooda/bootstrap/seed/oodac` (`878392` B, 2026-08-11):

| Probe | Result |
|-------|--------|
| `nm -S` | `0000000000456300 0000000000000caa T c_parse_secret_env` |
| `oo_str_concat` | **3** |
| `oo_str_slice` | **0** |
| `c_env_put` | **1** (no `__secref__` pair on this seed) |

Seed is also concat-era. Neither seed nor current product ELF is 7.10
machine-code proof.

### Floor (chs_rt, not primary) — note only
`runtime/chs_rt_str.c`:

- `oo_char_at` — heap 1-char (or UTF-8 1–4 byte) `OoStr` via `oo_str_alloc_payload`.
- `oo_str_concat` — heap copy of `a+b` (the **stale** ident path).
- `oo_str_slice` — heap copy of the `[start,end)` UTF-8 span (O(|ident|)),
  fail-soft empty on OOB — **what the new .oo will call after rebuild**.

There is **no** `c_parse_secret_env` in `chs_rt*.c` / `chs_rt.h`.

---
3. Re-emit residual (current host vs this .oo)
---

Isolated live emit (this pass):

```
ooda/oodac/oodac emit-c /tmp/s710_parse_only.oo   # extract of c_parse_secret_env only
```

- Prints preamble + proto + start of body, including the **new** shape:

```
OoStr needle = oo_str_concat(oo_str_lit("// "), oo_str_lit("SECRET:"));
...
  long long start = k;
while ((k < sn)) {
  OoStr c = oo_char_at(src, k);
ERR	c_emit	unknown free call needs annotation	oo_str_eq
```

- Dies at the untyped `let is_al = c == "_" || …` chain (same gate as
  7.1 `let is_start` / `is_cont`).

Gate: `c_emit_let_ext.oo` `c_emit_let_untyped_ty` — `c_rhs_call_name`
sees lowered `oo_str_eq(...)` and `oo_str_eq` is **not** on the
String/Int allowlist → `process_exit(1)`.

Honesty: **this host cannot re-emit the post-slice parser body** (stops
before `str_slice`). A rebuild that actually links Domain A's slice
needs a prior emit that already accepts the giant `||` as `long long`
(the 07:49 ELF was produced that way) **or** a typed `let is_al: Bool`
/ `char_is_alpha`/`char_is_digit` rewrite. Fail-closed (ERR line / emit
abort), not silent drop of the symbol.

Full-module `oodac emit-c oodac/c_emit_secret.oo` did not finish
preamble in 25s (4096 B truncated) — ignored as evidence.

Out of scope this auditor: annotate `let is_al: Bool`, allowlist
`oo_str_eq` as Int, or use preamble `char_is_alpha` / `char_is_digit`.

